# Development Standards

These standards exist to keep Project Codename organized, maintainable, and enjoyable to develop.

---

## Player Experience

- Every visible feature must provide value.
- No empty profession tabs.
- No "Coming Soon" placeholders.
- Aldren should always communicate naturally.
- The interface should remain clean and uncluttered.

---

## Development

- Every commit must leave the application working.
- Test before every commit.
- Push only after successful testing.
- Build one complete feature at a time.
- Avoid partially implemented systems.

---

## Code Organization

- One file, one responsibility.
- Organize by feature, not file size.
- Reuse existing systems whenever possible.
- Avoid duplicate logic.
- Keep future expansion in mind.

---

## Documentation

Major decisions belong in DECISIONS.md.

Long-term vision belongs in PROJECT-BIBLE.md.

Upcoming work belongs in ROADMAP.md.

Architecture changes belong in ARCHITECTURE.md.

Completed work belongs in CHANGELOG.md.

Current work belongs in TODO.md.

---

## Release Philosophy

Infrastructure improvements come before feature work.

Player-facing features are released only when complete.

Every release should leave the project in a better state than the previous one.

---

## Aldren

Aldren is the guide of Project Codename.

Other systems provide information.

Aldren provides understanding.

His purpose is to help the player make better decisions while reducing the need to use outside ESO resources.

---

## Project Goal

Build the best Elder Scrolls Online companion available.